Performance Optimization & Support of an Azure Data Platform
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Overview

This case study describes my experience supporting and optimizing a production data platform built on Microsoft Azure.

The platform integrates customer data from Salesforce into a centralized data warehouse and supports downstream analytics and web applications.

Although I did not design the architecture from scratch, I played a key role in database performance optimization and operational support, 
while gaining a deep understanding of the end-to-end data architecture.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Architecture Summary
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The platform follows a layered data architecture:

Data ingestion from Salesforce using Azure Data Factory
Staging and storage using Azure Blob Storage
Data warehouse hosted on Azure SQL Managed Instance
Data processing and analysis using Azure Databricks
Data consumption via web applications hosted on Azure App Service

This architecture supports batch ingestion, transformation, and reporting workloads.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data Flow
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Customer data is extracted from Salesforce using scheduled pipelines in Azure Data Factory
Data is stored in a staging layer in Blob Storage
Data is loaded into Azure SQL Managed Instance for structured storage
Azure Databricks is used for data transformation and analytical processing
Processed data is consumed by web applications and reporting tools

